INSERT INTO `articles` VALUES
(1,'FDA Grants Accelerated Approval for First-in-Class Targeted Oncology Therapy for Advanced Solid Tumors','fda-grants-accelerated-approval-targeted-oncology-therapy','The U.S. FDA has finalized an accelerated approval pathway for a novel dual-mechanism kinase inhibitor, opening treatment avenues for refractory solid tumors with specific genetic alterations.','<p>The United States Food and Drug Administration (FDA) today granted accelerated approval for a first-in-class small molecule kinase inhibitor indicated for adult patients with advanced, unresectable solid tumors harboring specific oncogenic pathway fusions.</p>\n      <h2>Clinical Efficacy and Trial Outcomes</h2>\n      <p>The landmark decision follows evaluation of multicenter Phase II trial data comprising 284 evaluable patients across 14 international trial sites. The confirmed overall response rate (ORR) reached 58.4%, with complete responses observed in 12.1% of patients. Median duration of response (DoR) exceeded 14.8 months.</p>\n      <blockquote>\"This regulatory milestone represents a paradigm shift in biomarker-driven precision oncology, where patient selection is guided strictly by genomic profiling rather than traditional tissue of origin,\" stated the Director of Oncology Center of Excellence.</blockquote>\n      <h2>Post-Marketing Commitments & Confirmatory Trials</h2>\n      <p>Under the accelerated approval provisions outlined in 21 CFR 314 Subpart H, the manufacturer is mandated to conduct and complete randomized controlled confirmatory Phase III studies to verify and describe clinical benefit, specifically measuring progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS).</p>\n      <p>Health systems and specialized oncology centers are advised to review updated prescribing guidelines regarding liver enzyme monitoring and dose adjustment protocols.</p>','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579684385127-1ef15d508118?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Biopharmaceutical laboratory precision research and oncology drug synthesis.','Published',1,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FDA Grants Accelerated Approval for First-in-Class Targeted Oncology Therapy | NewsKrez','FDA approves novel targeted kinase inhibitor for advanced solid tumors under accelerated pathway.',1,1,1,1420,4,'2026-11-17 18:29:21',NULL,'2026-11-18 01:59:21','2026-11-18 01:59:21','newskrez',NULL,NULL,'en','2026-11-18 08:34:41'),
(2,'FDA Clears AI-Powered Autonomous Cardiac Ultrasound System with Real-Time Guiding Algorithms','fda-clears-ai-cardiac-ultrasound-system-samd','In a landmark 510(k) clearance, the FDA has authorized an advanced Software as a Medical Device (SaMD) platform that directs bedside ultrasound probes and captures diagnostic-grade echocardiograms.','<p>Medical device regulators at the FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) have issued 510(k) clearance for a state-of-the-art cardiovascular imaging system powered by real-time deep learning navigation.</p>\n      <h2>Bridging Sonographer Shortages with Guided Diagnostics</h2>\n      <p>The system integrates real-time computer vision with point-of-care ultrasound (POCUS) transducers. As healthcare personnel position the probe on the patient\'s chest, on-screen dynamic vectors guide acoustic alignment to acquire standard diagnostic views including apical four-chamber and parasternal long-axis projections.</p>\n      <h2>Clinical Evaluation and Substantial Equivalence</h2>\n      <p>The premarket notification demonstrated substantial equivalence to predicate cardiovascular diagnostic imaging systems under 21 CFR 892.1600 (Product Code: IYO, Class II). Validation studies across three emergency departments and intensive care units proved image acquisition accuracy exceeding 94.6% among non-expert operators.</p>\n      <blockquote>\"AI-guided ultrasound democratization empowers critical care physicians and emergency teams to rapidly identify pericardial effusion and severe systolic dysfunction within seconds of patient presentation.\"</blockquote>','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1516549655169-df83a0774514?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Point-of-care cardiac ultrasound equipment utilized in modern acute clinical care.','Published',1,NULL,12,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FDA Clears AI Cardiac Ultrasound System Under 510(k) | NewsKrez','FDA 510(k) clearance issued for AI-guided echocardiography software facilitating point-of-care cardiac diagnostics.',0,1,1,2310,5,'2026-11-17 15:29:21',NULL,'2026-11-18 01:59:21','2026-11-18 01:59:21','newskrez',NULL,NULL,'en','2026-11-18 08:34:41'),
(3,'FDA Enacts Class I Urgent Recall for Infusion Pump Firmware Due to Upstream Occlusion Sensor Anomalies','urgent-class-i-recall-infusion-pump-firmware-safety','The FDA has classified a global recall of large-volume infusion pumps as Class I, warning that intermittent firmware sensor errors can cause unintended interruption of high-risk medication infusions.','<p>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration has posted an urgent Class I recall notice regarding select serial numbers of large-volume smart infusion pumps distributed worldwide. Class I recalls indicate situations where exposure to a violative product carries a reasonable probability of serious adverse health consequences or death.</p>\n      <h2>Root Cause Analysis</h2>\n      <p>Internal engineering evaluations and post-market surveillance alerts identified that a timing vulnerability within firmware versions 4.2.1 through 4.3.0 may fail to recognize upstream air-in-line or pressure occlusion alarms during micro-dose vasopressor administration.</p>\n      <h2>Action Steps for Biomedical Engineering Teams</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Immediately verify inventory against listed model identifiers and firmware builds.</li>\n        <li>Isolate unverified infusion units from critical care and pediatric units.</li>\n        <li>Apply manufacturer firmware patch v4.3.2 per field safety corrective action protocols.</li>\n        <li>Report any adverse events or infusion discrepancies to FDA MedWatch Form 3500A.</li>\n      </ul>','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1584515979956-d9f6e5d09982?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Hospital intravenous infusion delivery station and biomedical monitoring hardware.','Published',1,NULL,26,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Class I Medical Device Recall: Infusion Pump Sensor Firmware | NewsKrez','FDA declares Class I recall for smart infusion pumps due to sensor occlusion vulnerabilities.',1,0,0,980,3,'2026-11-17 12:29:21',NULL,'2026-11-18 01:59:21','2026-11-18 01:59:21','newskrez',NULL,NULL,'en','2026-11-18 08:34:41'),
(4,'WHO Issues Updated Pandemic Preparedness Guidance on Avian Influenza Surveillance Across Animal-Human Interfaces','who-guidance-avian-influenza-surveillance-pandemic-preparedness','The World Health Organization has issued technical recommendations to national ministries of health, urging aggressive genomic sequencing and occupational protection for dairy and poultry personnel.','<p>In an inter-agency briefing from Geneva, the World Health Organization (WHO), in coordination with WOAH and FAO, released comprehensive technical directives concerning the ongoing transboundary evolution of Highly Pathogenic Avian Influenza (HPAI) H5N1 clade 2.3.4.4b.</p>\n      <h2>Enhanced Genomic Sequencing Directives</h2>\n      <p>The guidance stresses prompt sharing of full-length viral gene sequences through public repositories such as GISAID to detect molecular signatures associated with mammalian adaptation, particularly mutations conferring increased affinity for alpha-2,6 sialic acid receptors in the human upper respiratory tract.</p>\n      <h2>Stockpiling Medical Countermeasures</h2>\n      <p>WHO highlighted the status of global pre-pandemic candidate vaccine viruses (CVVs) and recommended member states evaluate national reserves of neuraminidase inhibitors and baloxavir marboxil.</p>','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1584308666744-24d5c474f2ae?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','WHO global disease intelligence and laboratory diagnostic surveillance network.','Published',1,NULL,34,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'WHO Guidance on Avian Influenza Surveillance & Preparedness | NewsKrez','WHO releases comprehensive global guidance for avian influenza genomic monitoring and biosecurity.',0,1,0,1750,4,'2026-11-17 08:29:21',NULL,'2026-11-18 01:59:21','2026-11-18 01:59:21','newskrez',NULL,NULL,'en','2026-11-18 08:34:41'),
(5,'FDA Quality Management System Regulation (QMSR) Transition: Harmonizing 21 CFR Part 820 with ISO 13485:2016','fda-qmsr-transition-harmonizing-21-cfr-820-iso-13485','Global medical device manufacturers face critical deadlines as the FDA replaces legacy Good Manufacturing Practices (CGMP) with the modernized QMSR framework, aligning inspection criteria with ISO 13485.','<p>The United States FDA\'s final rule amending the medical device Quality System regulation (21 CFR Part 820) represents the most significant overhaul of device quality regulations in over three decades. Designated as the Quality Management System Regulation (QMSR), the rule harmonizes US requirements with the international standard ISO 13485:2016.</p>\n      <h2>Key Operational Adjustments for Device Manufacturers</h2>\n      <p>Quality and regulatory affairs leadership must adapt standard operating procedures across five core domains:</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><strong>Risk Management Across the Product Lifecycle:</strong> Direct incorporation of ISO 14971 risk management principles into design controls, supplier evaluations, and post-market vigilance.</li>\n        <li><strong>Clarified Terminology:</strong> Shifting from legacy terms such as \'DMR\' (Device Master Record) and \'DHR\' (Device History Record) to ISO standard documentation architectures.</li>\n        <li><strong>Supply Chain and Outsourced Process Controls:</strong> Rigorous vendor qualification requirements with documented traceability.</li>\n        <li><strong>Computer Software Assurance (CSA):</strong> Transitioning from cumbersome traditional CSV methodologies to risk-based, automated CSA testing.</li>\n      </ol>','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Quality management system documentation and regulatory inspection compliance audit.','Published',1,NULL,41,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'FDA QMSR Transition: Harmonizing 21 CFR 820 with ISO 13485 | NewsKrez','Detailed regulatory analysis of the FDA QMSR final rule harmonizing device manufacturing with ISO 13485.',0,0,1,3121,6,'2026-11-17 04:29:21',NULL,'2026-11-18 01:59:21','2026-11-18 02:27:58','newskrez',NULL,NULL,'en','2026-11-18 08:34:41'),
(6,'Generative AI in De Novo Molecular Design: Accelerating Small Molecule Hit-to-Lead Optimization','generative-ai-de-novo-molecular-design-drug-discovery','Computational chemistry platforms integrating transformer architectures and diffusion models are demonstrating unprecedented compression of pre-clinical discovery timelines from years to months.','<p>Biopharmaceutical research divisions are accelerating drug discovery pipelines through generative artificial intelligence models capable of designing drug-like molecules that bind with high affinity to previously \'undruggable\' biological targets.</p>\n      <h2>Deep Learning Models in Target Identification</h2>\n      <p>By leveraging 3D equivariant neural networks trained on crystallographic protein structures from the Protein Data Bank (PDB), the generative framework proposes stereochemically valid chemical scaffolds while simultaneously optimizing for ADMET (Absorption, Distribution, Metabolism, Excretion, and Toxicity) profiles.</p>\n      <p>Synthesizability filters prevent the generation of chemically intractable structures, enabling automated wet-lab robotic synthesis within 72 hours of algorithmic proposal.</p>','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507668077129-56e32842fceb?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','High-performance computational modeling of molecular docking and neural network representations.','Published',1,NULL,50,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Generative AI in De Novo Molecular Design & Drug Discovery | NewsKrez','How diffusion models and transformers are revolutionizing pharmaceutical drug discovery and hit-to-lead pipelines.',0,1,0,2040,5,'2026-11-17 00:29:21',NULL,'2026-11-18 01:59:21','2026-11-18 01:59:21','newskrez',NULL,NULL,'en','2026-11-18 08:34:41'),
(7,'FDA Class II: Victory Medical Center Pharmacy Recalls THYMOSIN ALPHA-1 (MDV) 3MG/ML **5ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Center Pharmacy, Aus','fda-recall-victory-medical-center-pharmacy-d-0145-2027-ac6186','Class II announced by FDA for THYMOSIN ALPHA-1 (MDV) 3MG/ML **5ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Center Pharmacy, Austin, Texas. Reason: Lack of Processing Controls...','\n      <p>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has posted an official drug enforcement report concerning <strong>Victory Medical Center Pharmacy</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Product and Classification Details</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> D-0145-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Recalling Firm:</strong> Victory Medical Center Pharmacy</li>\n        <li><strong>Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Enforcement Action</h2>\n      <p>Lack of Processing Controls</p>\n      <h2>Distribution Information</h2>\n      <p>CO, FL, TX</p>\n      <blockquote>Official notification published per FDA Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER) surveillance databases.</blockquote>\n    ','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1584308666744-24d5c474f2ae?w=1000&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Pharmaceutical product recall and laboratory testing.','Published',1,NULL,26,1,'https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-recalls#D-0145-2027','c1f5bb59775781b86ccfa23358c12bf9a40c101cc5dc694bf78b92ffa3d10690','D-0145-2027','https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-recalls#D-0145-2027','FDA Class II: Victory Medical Center Pharmacy Recalls THYMOS | NewsKrez','Class II announced by FDA for THYMOSIN ALPHA-1 (MDV) 3MG/ML **5ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Center Pharmacy, Austin, Texas. Reason: Lack of Processing Controls...',0,0,0,38,3,'2026-11-10 18:30:00',NULL,'2026-11-18 02:04:57','2026-11-18 02:04:57','newskrez',NULL,NULL,'en','2026-11-18 08:34:41'),
