(8,'FDA','recall','FDA Class II: Victory Medical Center Pharmacy Recalls TIRZEPATIDE/L-CARNITINE **10/50MG/ML** (MDV) **1ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Cente','fda-recall-victory-medical-center-pharmacy-d-0152-2027-ba5169','Class II announced by FDA for TIRZEPATIDE/L-CARNITINE **10/50MG/ML** (MDV) **1ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Center Pharmacy, Austin, Texas. Reason: Lack of Processing Controls...','\n      <p>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has posted an official drug enforcement report concerning <strong>Victory Medical Center Pharmacy</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Product and Classification Details</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> D-0152-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Recalling Firm:</strong> Victory Medical Center Pharmacy</li>\n        <li><strong>Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Enforcement Action</h2>\n      <p>Lack of Processing Controls</p>\n      <h2>Distribution Information</h2>\n      <p>CO, FL, TX</p>\n      <blockquote>Official notification published per FDA Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER) surveillance databases.</blockquote>\n    ','Class II','TIRZEPATIDE/L-CARNITINE **10/50MG/ML** (MDV) **1ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Center Pharmacy, Austin, Texas','Victory Medical Center Pharmacy','CO, FL, TX','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-recalls#D-0152-2027','D-0152-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:57','2026-11-18 02:04:57'),
(9,'FDA','recall','FDA Class II: Preferred Pharmaceuticals, Inc. Recalls Artificial Tears Lubricant Eye Drops, Visine, Pkg Size: 15, Mfg: Geri-Care: Broo','fda-recall-preferred-pharmaceuticals-inc-d-0158-2027-4caaeb','Class II announced by FDA for Artificial Tears Lubricant Eye Drops, Visine, Pkg Size: 15, Mfg: Geri-Care: Brooklyn, NY.  NDC: 68788-7266-0. Reason: Lack of Assurance of Sterility...','\n      <p>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has posted an official drug enforcement report concerning <strong>Preferred Pharmaceuticals, Inc.</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Product and Classification Details</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> D-0158-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Recalling Firm:</strong> Preferred Pharmaceuticals, Inc.</li>\n        <li><strong>Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Enforcement Action</h2>\n      <p>Lack of Assurance of Sterility</p>\n      <h2>Distribution Information</h2>\n      <p>U.S. Nationwide</p>\n      <blockquote>Official notification published per FDA Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER) surveillance databases.</blockquote>\n    ','Class II','Artificial Tears Lubricant Eye Drops, Visine, Pkg Size: 15, Mfg: Geri-Care: Brooklyn, NY.  NDC: 68788-7266-0','Preferred Pharmaceuticals, Inc.','U.S. Nationwide','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-recalls#D-0158-2027','D-0158-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:57','2026-11-18 02:04:57'),
(10,'FDA','recall','FDA Class II: American Health Packaging Recalls Cyanocobalamin Injection, USP, 1,000 mcg/mL, Rx Only, 25 x 1mL -Multiple-Dose Vi','fda-recall-american-health-packaging-d-0173-2027-3d86af','Class II announced by FDA for Cyanocobalamin Injection, USP, 1,000 mcg/mL, Rx Only, 25 x 1mL -Multiple-Dose Vials per carton, Mfg. by: American Regent. Reason: Presence of particulate matter:American Regent, Inc. notified BluePoint Pharmaceuticals Laboratories regarding potential glass particle contamination ...','\n      <p>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has posted an official drug enforcement report concerning <strong>American Health Packaging</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Product and Classification Details</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> D-0173-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Recalling Firm:</strong> American Health Packaging</li>\n        <li><strong>Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Enforcement Action</h2>\n      <p>Presence of particulate matter:American Regent, Inc. notified BluePoint Pharmaceuticals Laboratories regarding potential glass particle contamination (foreign glass fragment) identified in the product batch.</p>\n      <h2>Distribution Information</h2>\n      <p>Nationwide in the USA</p>\n      <blockquote>Official notification published per FDA Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER) surveillance databases.</blockquote>\n    ','Class II','Cyanocobalamin Injection, USP, 1,000 mcg/mL, Rx Only, 25 x 1mL -Multiple-Dose Vials per carton, Mfg. by: American Regent, Inc., For Bluepoint Laboratories. Carton NDC 68001-542-60; Vial NDC 68001-542-59','American Health Packaging','Nationwide in the USA','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-recalls#D-0173-2027','D-0173-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:57','2026-11-18 02:04:57'),
(11,'FDA','recall','FDA Class II: Victory Medical Center Pharmacy Recalls CJC-1295/IPAMORELIN (MDV) 2/2MG/ML **2ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Center Pharmacy','fda-recall-victory-medical-center-pharmacy-d-0124-2027-c2ae9d','Class II announced by FDA for CJC-1295/IPAMORELIN (MDV) 2/2MG/ML **2ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Center Pharmacy, Austin, Texas. Reason: Lack of Processing Controls...','\n      <p>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has posted an official drug enforcement report concerning <strong>Victory Medical Center Pharmacy</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Product and Classification Details</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> D-0124-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Recalling Firm:</strong> Victory Medical Center Pharmacy</li>\n        <li><strong>Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Enforcement Action</h2>\n      <p>Lack of Processing Controls</p>\n      <h2>Distribution Information</h2>\n      <p>CO, FL, TX</p>\n      <blockquote>Official notification published per FDA Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER) surveillance databases.</blockquote>\n    ','Class II','CJC-1295/IPAMORELIN (MDV) 2/2MG/ML **2ML**, VMC, Victory Medical Center Pharmacy, Austin, Texas','Victory Medical Center Pharmacy','CO, FL, TX','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-recalls#D-0124-2027','D-0124-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:57','2026-11-18 02:04:57'),
(12,'FDA','recall','FDA Class II: Fresenius Medical Care Renal Therapies Group, LLC Recalls DELFLEX Peritoneal Dialysis Solution with 4.25% Dextrose, Low Magnesium/ Low Cal','fda-recall-fresenius-medical-care-renal-therapies-group-llc-d-0171-2027-a9113d','Class II announced by FDA for DELFLEX Peritoneal Dialysis Solution with 4.25% Dextrose, Low Magnesium/ Low Calcium and Attached stay safe Exchange Set. Reason: Lack of Assurance of Sterility:complaints have been received related to potential leaks from small perforations in the print area on the primary bag i...','\n      <p>The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has posted an official drug enforcement report concerning <strong>Fresenius Medical Care Renal Therapies Group, LLC</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Product and Classification Details</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> D-0171-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Recalling Firm:</strong> Fresenius Medical Care Renal Therapies Group, LLC</li>\n        <li><strong>Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Enforcement Action</h2>\n      <p>Lack of Assurance of Sterility:complaints have been received related to potential leaks from small perforations in the print area on the primary bag in the affected lots.</p>\n      <h2>Distribution Information</h2>\n      <p>Nationwide in the USA.</p>\n      <blockquote>Official notification published per FDA Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER) surveillance databases.</blockquote>\n    ','Class II','DELFLEX Peritoneal Dialysis Solution with 4.25% Dextrose, Low Magnesium/ Low Calcium and Attached stay safe Exchange Set, 2,500 mL Single dose bag, Sterile and Non-Pyrogenic, Rx only, CAT.NO. 054-25324.  Fresenius Medical Care, Renal Therapies Group,','Fresenius Medical Care Renal Therapies Group, LLC','Nationwide in the USA.','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-safety-and-availability/drug-recalls#D-0171-2027','D-0171-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:57','2026-11-18 02:04:57'),
(13,'FDA','guidance','FDA CDRH 510(k) Clearance (K260132): Jason membrane by Botiss Biomaterials GmbH','fda-510k-k260132-jason-membrane-87c710','FDA issues 510(k) premarket notification clearance for Jason membrane (K260132) manufactured by Botiss Biomaterials GmbH.','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has finalized premarket notification review under Section 510(k) for <strong>Jason membrane</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Premarket Clearance Dossier</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Submission Number:</strong> K260132</li>\n        <li><strong>Applicant / Sponsor:</strong> Botiss Biomaterials GmbH</li>\n        <li><strong>Device Trade Name:</strong> Jason membrane</li>\n        <li><strong>Product Code:</strong> NPL</li>\n        <li><strong>Advisory Committee:</strong> Dental</li>\n        <li><strong>Regulatory Decision:</strong> Substantially Equivalent</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The FDA determined that the device is substantially equivalent to legally marketed predicate devices for the indications specified in the submission summary.</p>\n    ',NULL,'Jason membrane','Botiss Biomaterials GmbH',NULL,'2026-11-07 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfpmn/pmn.cfm?ID=K260132','K260132','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(14,'FDA','guidance','FDA CDRH 510(k) Clearance (K262755): Wave Electrode;Remote Wave Electrode by Bionit Labs Srl','fda-510k-k262755-wave-electroderemote-wave-electrode-a48fc3','FDA issues 510(k) premarket notification clearance for Wave Electrode;Remote Wave Electrode (K262755) manufactured by Bionit Labs Srl.','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has finalized premarket notification review under Section 510(k) for <strong>Wave Electrode;Remote Wave Electrode</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Premarket Clearance Dossier</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Submission Number:</strong> K262755</li>\n        <li><strong>Applicant / Sponsor:</strong> Bionit Labs Srl</li>\n        <li><strong>Device Trade Name:</strong> Wave Electrode;Remote Wave Electrode</li>\n        <li><strong>Product Code:</strong> GXY</li>\n        <li><strong>Advisory Committee:</strong> Neurology</li>\n        <li><strong>Regulatory Decision:</strong> Substantially Equivalent</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The FDA determined that the device is substantially equivalent to legally marketed predicate devices for the indications specified in the submission summary.</p>\n    ',NULL,'Wave Electrode;Remote Wave Electrode','Bionit Labs Srl',NULL,'2026-11-05 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfpmn/pmn.cfm?ID=K262755','K262755','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(15,'FDA','guidance','FDA CDRH 510(k) Clearance (K260674): Atellica IM Vitamin D Total II (VitDII) by Siemens Healthcare Diagnostics, Inc.','fda-510k-k260674-atellica-im-vitamin-d-total-ii-vitdii-82caa2','FDA issues 510(k) premarket notification clearance for Atellica IM Vitamin D Total II (VitDII) (K260674) manufactured by Siemens Healthcare Diagnostics, Inc..','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has finalized premarket notification review under Section 510(k) for <strong>Atellica IM Vitamin D Total II (VitDII)</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Premarket Clearance Dossier</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Submission Number:</strong> K260674</li>\n        <li><strong>Applicant / Sponsor:</strong> Siemens Healthcare Diagnostics, Inc.</li>\n        <li><strong>Device Trade Name:</strong> Atellica IM Vitamin D Total II (VitDII)</li>\n        <li><strong>Product Code:</strong> MRG</li>\n        <li><strong>Advisory Committee:</strong> Clinical Chemistry</li>\n        <li><strong>Regulatory Decision:</strong> Substantially Equivalent</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The FDA determined that the device is substantially equivalent to legally marketed predicate devices for the indications specified in the submission summary.</p>\n    ',NULL,'Atellica IM Vitamin D Total II (VitDII)','Siemens Healthcare Diagnostics, Inc.',NULL,'2026-11-05 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfpmn/pmn.cfm?ID=K260674','K260674','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
