(17,'FDA','guidance','FDA CDRH 510(k) Clearance (K263749): CadAI-B Dx by BeamWorks, Inc.','fda-510k-k263749-cadai-b-dx-734a42','FDA issues 510(k) premarket notification clearance for CadAI-B Dx (K263749) manufactured by BeamWorks, Inc..','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has finalized premarket notification review under Section 510(k) for <strong>CadAI-B Dx</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Premarket Clearance Dossier</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Submission Number:</strong> K263749</li>\n        <li><strong>Applicant / Sponsor:</strong> BeamWorks, Inc.</li>\n        <li><strong>Device Trade Name:</strong> CadAI-B Dx</li>\n        <li><strong>Product Code:</strong> QDQ</li>\n        <li><strong>Advisory Committee:</strong> Radiology</li>\n        <li><strong>Regulatory Decision:</strong> Substantially Equivalent</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The FDA determined that the device is substantially equivalent to legally marketed predicate devices for the indications specified in the submission summary.</p>\n    ',NULL,'CadAI-B Dx','BeamWorks, Inc.',NULL,'2026-11-05 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfpmn/pmn.cfm?ID=K263749','K263749','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(18,'FDA','guidance','FDA CDRH 510(k) Clearance (K260478): CleanBreak by Icu Medical, Inc.','fda-510k-k260478-cleanbreak-4a2209','FDA issues 510(k) premarket notification clearance for CleanBreak (K260478) manufactured by Icu Medical, Inc..','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has finalized premarket notification review under Section 510(k) for <strong>CleanBreak</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Premarket Clearance Dossier</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Submission Number:</strong> K260478</li>\n        <li><strong>Applicant / Sponsor:</strong> Icu Medical, Inc.</li>\n        <li><strong>Device Trade Name:</strong> CleanBreak</li>\n        <li><strong>Product Code:</strong> QOI</li>\n        <li><strong>Advisory Committee:</strong> General Hospital</li>\n        <li><strong>Regulatory Decision:</strong> Substantially Equivalent</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The FDA determined that the device is substantially equivalent to legally marketed predicate devices for the indications specified in the submission summary.</p>\n    ',NULL,'CleanBreak','Icu Medical, Inc.',NULL,'2026-11-05 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfpmn/pmn.cfm?ID=K260478','K260478','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(19,'FDA','guidance','FDA CDRH 510(k) Clearance (K262329): Electric Wheelchair (MK100W(6012A), MK100W(6016A), MK100W(9005), MK100W(9006)) by MAIKANG MEDICAL EQUIPMENT (HEBEI) CO., Ltd.','fda-510k-k262329-electric-wheelchair-mk100w6012a-mk100w6016a-mk100w9005-mk100w90-e7da26','FDA issues 510(k) premarket notification clearance for Electric Wheelchair (MK100W(6012A), MK100W(6016A), MK100W(9005), MK100W(9006)) (K262329) manufactured by MAIKANG MEDICAL EQUIPMENT (HEBEI) CO., Ltd..','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has finalized premarket notification review under Section 510(k) for <strong>Electric Wheelchair (MK100W(6012A), MK100W(6016A), MK100W(9005), MK100W(9006))</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Premarket Clearance Dossier</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Submission Number:</strong> K262329</li>\n        <li><strong>Applicant / Sponsor:</strong> MAIKANG MEDICAL EQUIPMENT (HEBEI) CO., Ltd.</li>\n        <li><strong>Device Trade Name:</strong> Electric Wheelchair (MK100W(6012A), MK100W(6016A), MK100W(9005), MK100W(9006))</li>\n        <li><strong>Product Code:</strong> ITI</li>\n        <li><strong>Advisory Committee:</strong> Physical Medicine</li>\n        <li><strong>Regulatory Decision:</strong> Substantially Equivalent</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The FDA determined that the device is substantially equivalent to legally marketed predicate devices for the indications specified in the submission summary.</p>\n    ',NULL,'Electric Wheelchair (MK100W(6012A), MK100W(6016A), MK100W(9005), MK100W(9006))','MAIKANG MEDICAL EQUIPMENT (HEBEI) CO., Ltd.',NULL,'2026-11-05 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfpmn/pmn.cfm?ID=K262329','K262329','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(20,'FDA','recall','FDA Medical Device Class II: Henry Schein Inc. – Generic Name: Perma Sharp Sutures;  Generic Name: Polypropylene Nonabsorbable Su','fda-device-recall-henry-schein-inc-z-0346-2027-e4d4d6','Class II issued for Generic Name: Perma Sharp Sutures;  Generic Name: Polypropylene Nonabsorbable Surgical Suture;  Model/Catalog Number: PS. Products lack 510(k) clearance....','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has issued an official medical device recall determination for <strong>Generic Name: Perma Sharp Sutures;  Generic Name: Polypropylene Nonabsorbable Surgical Suture;  Model/Catalog Number: PSN8695P (HSI Item No. 600-9795);  Product Description: Sterile, synthetic, nonabsorbable, monofilament 6-0 blue polypropylene surgical suture, 18-inch length, with C-3 premium surgical needle.  Component: N/A;</strong> produced by <strong>Henry Schein Inc.</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Regulatory Recall Specification</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> Z-0346-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Recall Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Firm Name:</strong> Henry Schein Inc.</li>\n        <li><strong>Current Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Device Recall</h2>\n      <p>Products lack 510(k) clearance.</p>\n      <h2>Clinical & Corrective Actions</h2>\n      <p>Healthcare facilities and clinical engineering departments are advised to review the affected serial numbers and follow the manufacturer\'s field safety notice instructions.</p>\n    ','Class II','Generic Name: Perma Sharp Sutures;  Generic Name: Polypropylene Nonabsorbable Surgical Suture;  Model/Catalog Number: PSN8695P (HSI Item No. 600-9795);  Product Description: Sterile, synthetic, nonabsorbable, monofilament 6-0 blue polypropylene surgi','Henry Schein Inc.','Worldwide distribution - U.S. Nationwide and the countries of Canada, Uganda, and the Cayman Islands.','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfres/res.cfm?id=Z-0346-2027','Z-0346-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(21,'FDA','recall','FDA Medical Device Class II: GE Medical Systems, LLC – Senographe Pristina','fda-device-recall-ge-medical-systems-llc-z-0327-2027-231e33','Class II issued for Senographe Pristina. GE HealthCare has become aware of a nonconformance to certain Senographe Pristina VIA systems. Specifically, in cases of 3D+2D manual mode w...','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has issued an official medical device recall determination for <strong>Senographe Pristina</strong> produced by <strong>GE Medical Systems, LLC</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Regulatory Recall Specification</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> Z-0327-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Recall Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Firm Name:</strong> GE Medical Systems, LLC</li>\n        <li><strong>Current Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Device Recall</h2>\n      <p>GE HealthCare has become aware of a nonconformance to certain Senographe Pristina VIA systems. Specifically, in cases of 3D+2D manual mode where the acquisition configuration of the anode track/filter combination is different, it can result in the following:  the collimator blades might be visible in the image, or the collimator might be open more than expected, and  an incorrect collimator filter might be used with respect to the anode track selected  This issue could result in a minor additional X-ray dose being delivered to the patient and obvious artifacts in the image (collimator blades).</p>\n      <h2>Clinical & Corrective Actions</h2>\n      <p>Healthcare facilities and clinical engineering departments are advised to review the affected serial numbers and follow the manufacturer\'s field safety notice instructions.</p>\n    ','Class II','Senographe Pristina','GE Medical Systems, LLC','USA and OUS.','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfres/res.cfm?id=Z-0327-2027','Z-0327-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(22,'FDA','recall','FDA Medical Device Class II: Henry Schein Inc. – Generic Name: Perma Sharp Sutures;  Generic Name: Polypropylene Nonabsorbable Su','fda-device-recall-henry-schein-inc-z-0342-2027-bb557c','Class II issued for Generic Name: Perma Sharp Sutures;  Generic Name: Polypropylene Nonabsorbable Surgical Suture;  Model/Catalog Number: PS. Products lack 510(k) clearance....','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has issued an official medical device recall determination for <strong>Generic Name: Perma Sharp Sutures;  Generic Name: Polypropylene Nonabsorbable Surgical Suture;  Model/Catalog Number: PSN8384P (HSI Item No. 600-7664);  Product Description: Sterile, synthetic, nonabsorbable, monofilament 6-0 blue polypropylene surgical suture, 18-inch length, with C-17 3/8-circle surgical needle.  Component: N/A;</strong> produced by <strong>Henry Schein Inc.</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Regulatory Recall Specification</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> Z-0342-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Recall Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Firm Name:</strong> Henry Schein Inc.</li>\n        <li><strong>Current Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Device Recall</h2>\n      <p>Products lack 510(k) clearance.</p>\n      <h2>Clinical & Corrective Actions</h2>\n      <p>Healthcare facilities and clinical engineering departments are advised to review the affected serial numbers and follow the manufacturer\'s field safety notice instructions.</p>\n    ','Class II','Generic Name: Perma Sharp Sutures;  Generic Name: Polypropylene Nonabsorbable Surgical Suture;  Model/Catalog Number: PSN8384P (HSI Item No. 600-7664);  Product Description: Sterile, synthetic, nonabsorbable, monofilament 6-0 blue polypropylene surgi','Henry Schein Inc.','Worldwide distribution - U.S. Nationwide and the countries of Canada, Uganda, and the Cayman Islands.','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfres/res.cfm?id=Z-0342-2027','Z-0342-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(23,'FDA','recall','FDA Medical Device Class I: Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc. – Tandem Mobi Insulin Pump, Models: 1004004, 1010750, 1012676, 1012719, 1013655, 1','fda-device-recall-tandem-diabetes-care-inc-z-0316-2027-6ff46b','Class I issued for Tandem Mobi Insulin Pump, Models: 1004004, 1010750, 1012676, 1012719, 1013655, 1013656, 1013501, 1013700, 1014081, 10148. Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc. ( Tandem ) has identified that certain Tandem Mobi insulin pumps may generate false-positive occlusion alarms whe...','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has issued an official medical device recall determination for <strong>Tandem Mobi Insulin Pump, Models: 1004004, 1010750, 1012676, 1012719, 1013655, 1013656, 1013501, 1013700, 1014081, 1014801, 1014811, 1014813, 1014936, 1016911, 1016912, 1016913, 1016914, 1018075, 1018077, 1018078</strong> produced by <strong>Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc.</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Regulatory Recall Specification</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> Z-0316-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Recall Classification:</strong> Class I</li>\n        <li><strong>Firm Name:</strong> Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc.</li>\n        <li><strong>Current Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Device Recall</h2>\n      <p>Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc. ( Tandem ) has identified that certain Tandem Mobi insulin pumps may generate false-positive occlusion alarms when no actual insulin flow obstruction is present. Investigation determined that increased friction within the drive module can reduce available motor power and, under certain conditions, cause motor speed to fall below the occlusion detection threshold. As a result, the pump may incorrectly detect an occlusion condition and suspend insulin delivery.     When an occlusion alarm occurs, insulin delivery remains suspended until the user acknowledges the alarm and resumes therapy. Repeated false-positive occlusion alarms, if not addressed promptly, may result in interruptions of insulin delivery that can increase the risk of elevated blood glucose levels. In severe cases, hyperglycemia may require medical intervention or hospitalization.</p>\n      <h2>Clinical & Corrective Actions</h2>\n      <p>Healthcare facilities and clinical engineering departments are advised to review the affected serial numbers and follow the manufacturer\'s field safety notice instructions.</p>\n    ','Class I','Tandem Mobi Insulin Pump, Models: 1004004, 1010750, 1012676, 1012719, 1013655, 1013656, 1013501, 1013700, 1014081, 1014801, 1014811, 1014813, 1014936, 1016911, 1016912, 1016913, 1016914, 1018075, 1018077, 1018078','Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc.','Worldwide - US Nationwide distribution including in the states of CA, FL, NC, OK, UT, WA, IL, PA, MN, VA, NY, IN, HI, OR, GA, MI, KS, CO, WI, SC, null, TX, NE, AZ, OH, NM, NV, MA, SD, IA, TN, ID, MD, RI, CT, NJ, ME, KY, MT, WV, VT, MS, AR, AL, DC, LA, MO, NH, PR, ND, AK, DE, WY and the country of Canada.','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfres/res.cfm?id=Z-0316-2027','Z-0316-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(24,'FDA','recall','FDA Medical Device Class I: Cardinal Health 200, LLC – Cardinal Health Presource PBDS kits, Containing BD Alaris Pump Infusion Sets use','fda-device-recall-cardinal-health-200-llc-z-0216-2027-41c692','Class I issued for Cardinal Health Presource PBDS kits, Containing BD Alaris Pump Infusion Sets used with BD Alaris Pump Module Model 8100,. Kits contain infusion sets which were recalled for performance issues....','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has issued an official medical device recall determination for <strong>Cardinal Health Presource PBDS kits, Containing BD Alaris Pump Infusion Sets used with BD Alaris Pump Module Model 8100, labeled as:    1) KIT,C SECTION ADMIT,, CATALOG # MATJV8300D;   2) KIT,C SECTION ADMIT,, CATALOG # MATJV8300C;   3) KIT, EMERGENCY C SECTION ADMIT, CATALOG # MAT216337B;   4) IN PATIENT KIT   , CATALOG # PG21OTAUHA.</strong> produced by <strong>Cardinal Health 200, LLC</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Regulatory Recall Specification</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> Z-0216-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Recall Classification:</strong> Class I</li>\n        <li><strong>Firm Name:</strong> Cardinal Health 200, LLC</li>\n        <li><strong>Current Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Device Recall</h2>\n      <p>Kits contain infusion sets which were recalled for performance issues.</p>\n      <h2>Clinical & Corrective Actions</h2>\n      <p>Healthcare facilities and clinical engineering departments are advised to review the affected serial numbers and follow the manufacturer\'s field safety notice instructions.</p>\n    ','Class I','Cardinal Health Presource PBDS kits, Containing BD Alaris Pump Infusion Sets used with BD Alaris Pump Module Model 8100, labeled as:    1) KIT,C SECTION ADMIT,, CATALOG # MATJV8300D;   2) KIT,C SECTION ADMIT,, CATALOG # MATJV8300C;   3) KIT, EMERGENC','Cardinal Health 200, LLC','US and Canada','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfres/res.cfm?id=Z-0216-2027','Z-0216-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
(25,'FDA','recall','FDA Medical Device Class II: Baxter Healthcare Corporation – TruSystem 7500 Hybrid Plus (FC), Fixed-Installation Operating Table Column, Mode','fda-device-recall-baxter-healthcare-corporation-z-0354-2027-b42ecf','Class II issued for TruSystem 7500 Hybrid Plus (FC), Fixed-Installation Operating Table Column, Model/Catalog Number: 1854087. There is an issue with the main lift mechanism. The main lift may unexpectedly drop from its set position to its lowest position during use....','\n      <p>The FDA Center for Devices and Radiological Health (CDRH) has issued an official medical device recall determination for <strong>TruSystem 7500 Hybrid Plus (FC), Fixed-Installation Operating Table Column, Model/Catalog Number: 1854087</strong> produced by <strong>Baxter Healthcare Corporation</strong>.</p>\n      <h2>Regulatory Recall Specification</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Recall Number:</strong> Z-0354-2027</li>\n        <li><strong>Recall Classification:</strong> Class II</li>\n        <li><strong>Firm Name:</strong> Baxter Healthcare Corporation</li>\n        <li><strong>Current Status:</strong> Ongoing</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h2>Reason for Device Recall</h2>\n      <p>There is an issue with the main lift mechanism. The main lift may unexpectedly drop from its set position to its lowest position during use. In these cases, the tabletop could not be raised again after the drop occurred. The issue has been associated with unexpected wear of the main lift assembly, also known as the telescopic spindle. An uncontrolled drop of the surgical table may result in an abrupt patient displacement during surgery. Serious or critical adverse health consequences may occur, including traumatic injury, airway compromise, and surgical procedure complications, among others. Baxter has received three complaints related to this issue, with no reported patient injury.</p>\n      <h2>Clinical & Corrective Actions</h2>\n      <p>Healthcare facilities and clinical engineering departments are advised to review the affected serial numbers and follow the manufacturer\'s field safety notice instructions.</p>\n    ','Class II','TruSystem 7500 Hybrid Plus (FC), Fixed-Installation Operating Table Column, Model/Catalog Number: 1854087','Baxter Healthcare Corporation','Worldwide - US Nationwide distribution.','2026-11-10 18:30:00','https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfres/res.cfm?id=Z-0354-2027','Z-0354-2027','active','2026-11-18 02:04:58','2026-11-18 02:04:58'),
